n the Cape Bon Peninsula, birthplace of the condiment, with Nabeul famous for being the primary center for its production. The main ingredients are roasted red peppers, Baklouti peppers, spices and herbs such as garlic paste, caraway seeds, coriander seeds, cumin and olive oil to carry the oil-soluble flavors."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-harissa"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harissa"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Belgian cuisine","cuisine/belgian-cuisine",[["Algérienne sauce","dish/algerienne-sauce"],["Samurai sauce","dish/samurai-sauce"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Mayonnaise","ingredient/mayonnaise"],["Ketchup","ingredient/ketchup"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/0/05/%D9%87%D8%B1%D9%8A%D8%B3%D8%A9_%D8%AF%D9%8A%D8%A7%D8%B1%D9%8A.JPG/500px-%D9%87%D8%B1%D9%8A%D8%B3%D8%A9_%D8%AF%D9%8A%D8%A7%D8%B1%D9%8A.JPG","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Ovva olfa","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D9%87%D8%B1%D9%8A%D8%B3%D8%A9_%D8%AF%D9%8A%D8%A7%D8%B1%D9%8A.JPG"}},"ingredient/syrup":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/syrup","n":"Syrup","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 7 dishes across 9 cuisines","intro":[["In cooking, syrup is a thick, viscous, liquid condiment consisting primarily of a solution of sugar in water. It typically contains a large amount of dissolved sugars but shows little tendency to deposit crystals. In its concentrated form, its consistency is similar to that of molasses. The viscosity arises from the multiple hydrogen bonds between the dissolved sugar, which has many hydroxyl (OH) groups."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-syrup"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syrup"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":9,"groups":[["Azerbaijani cuisine","cuisine/azerbai