 ceremonies."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-sholezard"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sholezard"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Iranian cuisine","cuisine/iranian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":7,"links":[["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Cardamom","ingredient/cardamom"],["Cinnamon","ingredient/cinnamon"],["Coffee","ingredient/coffee"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Rose water","ingredient/rose-water"],["Saffron","ingredient/saffron"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Unicorns in the Kitchen","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"unicornsinthekitchen.com","note":"Iranian-born Shadi HasanzadeNemati's blog with a large Persian recipe section.","url":"https://www.unicornsinthekitchen.com/persian-recipes","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Iranian cuisine","links":[["Akuri","dish/akuri"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Chelow kabab","dish/chelow-kabab"],["Doogh","dish/doogh"],["Falooda","dish/falooda"],["Jujeh kabab","dish/jujeh-kabab"],["Kabab torsh","dish/kabab-torsh"],["Keşkek","dish/keskek"],["Khash (dish)","dish/khash-dish"],["Khoresh karafs","dish/khoresh-karafs"],["Lighvan cheese","dish/lighvan-cheese"],["Nisholda","dish/nisholda"],["Pilaf","dish/pilaf"],["Scorched rice","dish/scorched-rice"],["Sheermal","dish/sheermal"],["Shirazi salad","dish/shirazi-salad"],["Shirin polo","dish/shirin-polo"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/1/10/Shole-zrad-2014.JPG/500px-Shole-zrad-2014.JPG","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Rezarad","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shole-zrad-2014.JPG"}},"ingredient/sweet-corn":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/sweet-corn","n":"Sweet corn","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 2 cuisines","intro":[["Sweet corn (Zea mays convar. saccharata var. rugosa), also called sweetcorn, sugar corn, pole corn, or simply corn is a variety of corn (maize) grown for human consumption with a relatively high sugar content."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-sweet-corn"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweet_corn"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Succotash","dish/succotash"]]],["Wampanoag foodways","cuisine/wampanoag-foodways",[["Succotash","dish/succotash"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Bell peppers","ingredient/bell-peppers"],["Black pepper","ingredient/black-pepper"],["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Edible salt","ingredient/edible-salt"],["Lima bean","ingredient/lima-bean"],["Tomatoes","ingredient/tomatoes"],["Zea mays Saccharata Group","ingredient/zea-mays-saccharata-group"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/7/79/VegCorn.jpg/500px-VegCorn.jpg","w":500,"h":329,"by":"The original Uploader was wstoakLL at English Wikipedia","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:VegCorn.jpg"}},"ingredient/prunes":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/prunes","n":"Prunes","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 2 cuisines","intro":[["A prune is a dried plum, made by pruny prunipulus most commonly from the European plum (Prunus domestica) tree. Not all plum species or varieties can be dried into prunes. Use of the term prune for fresh plums is obsolete except when applied to varieties of plum grown for drying. In this usage, a prune is the firm-fleshed plum fruit of P. domestica varieties that have a high soluble solids content and do not ferment during drying."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-prunes"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prunes"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["Algerian cuisine","cuisine/algerian-cuisine",[["Tajine lham-lahlou","dish/tajine-lham-lahlou"]]],["Moroccan cuisine","cuisine/moroccan-cuisine",[["Tajine lham-lahlou","dish/tajine-lham-lahlou"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Apricots","ingredient/apricots"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/9/97/Rosales_-_Dried_Prunus_domestica_d.jpg/500px-Rosales_-_Dried_Prunus_domestica_d.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Emőke Dénes","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rosales_-_Dried_Prunus_domestica_d.jpg"}},"dish/tshai-bue-thng":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/tshai-bue-thng","n":"Tshài-bué-thng","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Chinese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Tshài-bué-thng is a traditional Taiwanese soup made by combining the leftover ingredients and dishes from a large Taiwanese banquet (known as Pān-toh). The soup typically blends assorted meats, seafood, bamboo shoots, shiitake mushrooms, vegetables, and rich broths into a complex stew-like soup. It is often regarded as the Taiwanese take of the Chinese dish Buddha Jumps Over the Wall and the American dish Mulligan stew."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-tshai-bue-thng"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tsh%C3%A0i-bu%C3%A9-thng"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Brassica juncea","ingredient/brassica-juncea"],["Garcinia atroviridis","ingredient/garcinia-atroviridis"],["Leftovers","ingredient/leftovers"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"The Woks of Life","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"thewoksoflife.com","note":"Chinese and Chinese American recipes from the Leung family, running since 2013.","url":"https://thewoksoflife.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Chinese Cooking Demystified","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"youtube.com","note":"Technique-heavy YouTube channel on regional Chinese home and restaurant cooking.","url":"https://www.y